; Leg GB -- the host SENDS.  CKFCMID RECEIVES with --rtscts.  THE LEG.
;
; WHY THE MARKS MOVED.  SS16ak ran this at 256/64 and the leg went
; off-shape: a timeout and three retransmissions inside the first 7,680
; bytes, and rxpeak latched fourteen bytes into a RESEND, which is the one
; place SS16m and SS16ag say rxpeak means nothing.  A 64-byte release point
; means each hold-off lasts until 192 bytes have drained, ~93 ms, over and
; over -- enough to disturb C-Kermit's round-trip estimator during slow
; start.
;
; 1024/896 is a NARROW BAND instead of a low mark: each pause is 128 bytes
; of drain, about 62 ms, and the assert fires often.  Short pauses, same
; mechanism.
;
; AND THE READING IS NOW A CAP, NOT A COMPARISON, which is why a
; retransmission cannot void this leg the way it voided DB:
;
;     rxpeak ~1,0xx-1,4xx   occupancy PINNED at the mark.  The far end
;                           stopped when we asked.  RTS IS WIRED OUTBOUND.
;     rxpeak ~2,8xx-3,1xx   occupancy followed GA's curve.  We asserted
;                           (held>0) and nothing happened.
;
; ALWAYS run mapoffset.py on peakat before believing rxpeak:
;     python3 v9k/tools/mapoffset.py s16alGB.pkt --rxbytes <n> <peakat>
; A peak inside a resend is not a measurement of anything.
;
; held/rel say WE asserted and must END EQUAL.  rxpeak says THEY listened.
set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set retry 30
set parity none
set flow rts/cts
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16alGB.pkt
send rcvgb.dat
statistics
